  "note": "Zoladex 3.6 mg is still on the PBS (item 1454M, for other conditions, not gender dysphoria). It was due to leave on 1 November 2026, but the PBS Summary of Changes for 1 November 2026 lists no change to it and no deletion notice. AstraZeneca says it will stay on the PBS until 1 May 2027, that PBS prescriptions written by 30 April 2027 can be filled until 1 May 2028, and that the free Zoladex Continuity Program will not go ahead. Ask the pharmacist for the current position. Triptorelin 3.75 mg (Diphereline) has had no PBS restriction since 1 October 2026, but its listing is \"not for use in gender dysphoria in minors\".",
